{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountHealth"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MountHealth","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mount can be present in the kernel’s mount table and still be unusable — the rclone"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server behind it may have died, or the connection may have been severed by sleep. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mount table alone therefore cannot answer “is this working?”; something has to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"actually touch the filesystem."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Touching it is the dangerous part. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against a wedged NFS mount blocks until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the soft-mount timeout expires, so every probe runs on a detached task with a deadline","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the caller can abandon. Nothing here may ever be awaited from the main actor without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that deadline.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountHealth\/backoff(attempt:)","doc:\/\/docs.GrrCloneCore\/documentation\/GrrCloneCore\/MountHealth\/probe(_:timeout:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"},{"title":"Enumera